From 284fa77c434c77485b5cead17298041ee8651cbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:30:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: scope allocator-wide shared admission to MoE NVMe
 streaming

The MoE pick (1dd2bb6f7a) put arifi_vk_shared_reserve on every host-visible
buffer allocation, default on for every model. On the X1 qwen4exp dense load
(mmap + lazy, ~6 GiB available) it refused a 993280-byte planned staging buffer
(available 5.97 GiB minus a 6 GiB reserve = 0) and the uncaught vk::SystemError
killed llama-server (lane-298 ismoke-10061217 arm ig2, 0xC0000409). Off Windows
the probe returns 0, so shared growth failed closed for every model.

Admission now applies when GGML_ARIFI_MOE_NVME=1 (every measured MoE streaming
arm); GGML_ARIFI_VK_SHARED_ADMIT=1|0 forces it on or off. MoE streaming
behaviour is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - fork-authored (lane-298); no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: correctness fix (integ load regression), no speed claim: RED ismoke-10061217 arm ig2 / GREEN ismoke-10061337 (cache/mtp-x1-lane/cells)
---
 docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md                         |  3 +++
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp     | 12 ++++++++----
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-shared-budget.h | 11 +++++++++++
 3 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md b/docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
index 8b33534231..6e60be63e3 100644
--- a/docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
+++ b/docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
@@ -182,6 +182,9 @@ with live available-RAM-minus-4-GiB admission and an 11800 MiB maximum.
 `GGML_ARIFI_VK_FILE_CACHE_RESERVE_MIB` defaults to an estimated 2048 MiB mapping
 window; streaming cells set zero because weight reads bypass the page cache.
 Pure device-local allocations share a 70 GiB lease ledger across backend and cache.
+The allocator-wide shared admission applies only when `GGML_ARIFI_MOE_NVME=1`;
+`GGML_ARIFI_VK_SHARED_ADMIT=1|0` forces it on or off for any model (lane-298 integ:
+default-on refused a 1 MB staging buffer on a dense qwen4exp load at 5.97 GiB available).
 
 `GGML_CUDA_MOE_CACHE_STATS=N` logs cumulative counters every N collected nodes.
 NVMe bytes/seconds describe successful aligned expert reads only; they exclude
